  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The molecule&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is having two sigma bond pairs and lone pair, hence, it exhibits angular or V-shape structure. The molecule&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is having two sigma bond pairs and a lone pair&nbsp;hence, it exhibits angular or V-shape structure. So, both molecules are having same shape. But double bond-double bond repulsions are greater than single bond repulsions, hence, the bond angle in sulphur dioxide is greater than water.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6afb167a-081d-40da-bbdd-75c339dc3af8.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 104px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;both have V-Shape&nbsp;</p><p>Bond angle: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p>",
